---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - projecttrack.dev" description="Why this project track exists and who built it.">
  <article class="about">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Why this track exists</h1>

    <p>Taking a Data Science degree that leans heavy on theory and light on application? Here is what helped.</p>

    <p>
      My own degree is strong on theory: statistics, the math behind the models, the algorithms. It doesn't leave
      much room for actually building something end to end.
    </p>

    <p>
      To get that practice, I worked through applied projects outside of class, mostly from a coding program I
      took, plus a couple of my own. Doing the work myself, and having to make it hold up on my own, is what
      actually taught me the parts a lecture doesn't cover.
    </p>

    <p>
      This track is a version of that: the kind of projects that helped, and the self-check approach I used to
      know if a project was actually done right, not just finished. I'm sharing it so the next cohort has a map
      instead of starting cold.
    </p>

    <p>
      A couple of things worth saying plainly. I didn't invent these kinds of projects. Task types like these
      exist all over the field. And this isn't a claim that I've landed a job because of it. This is my own track,
      written from scratch in my own words. It is not any institution's curriculum, and finishing it is not
      endorsed by anyone but me.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 5vw 120px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(30px, 4.2vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    color: var(--color-heading);
  }
  p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }
  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
